"""Editorial questions for historical video games and tabletop play."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


RETRO = """history_origins|How an Early Game Was Made|Which hardware, team, and market conditions shaped one original release?|Compare dated builds, manuals, credits, and developer records.
famous_examples|A Classic Game in Its Time|Why did one game stand out to its original players?|Compare contemporary reviews, sales evidence, competitors, and original hardware.
hidden_stories|The People Missing From Game Credits|Whose porting, testing, localization, or manufacturing work was omitted?|Use credits, contracts, oral histories, and build records.
beginner_explainers|Playing the Original Version|Which rules, controls, and display conditions define one historical game?|Document a named build and platform before explaining play.
advanced_concepts|Hardware Shapes Design|How did memory, input, display, or storage limits influence one mechanic?|Compare source or technical records with released behavior.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Lost or Disputed Version|What evidence supports claims about an unreleased game build?|Compare prototypes, catalogues, interviews, and provenance gaps.
technology_innovation|A Console Feature Changes Play|Did one hardware capability enable a new game design?|Compare dated software and contemporary technical documentation.
people_personalities|A Developer's Choice Under Constraint|Which alternatives did a named developer consider for one mechanic?|Use notes and collaborators' accounts without lone-genius claims.
major_events|A Game's Release Turning Point|How did one launch, recall, or platform change affect a title?|Trace dated distribution, reviews, revisions, and player access.
how_it_works|Inside a Classic Mechanic|How does one rule respond to player input in the original build?|Explain state and feedback conceptually using authorized evidence.
rise_fall|Why an Arcade or Platform Declined|Which factors explain changing use of one game format?|Compare costs, home alternatives, policy, and user accounts.
then_vs_now|Original Versus Remaster|What changed in rules, image, sound, timing, and rights?|Compare specific builds on matched hardware where possible.
future_developments|Preserving a Playable Game|What materials would let future researchers understand one old game?|Assess original media, hardware, source, manual, captures, and legal access.
myths_vs_facts|The First Video Game Claim|Does a first-ever claim depend on how game or commercial release is defined?|Compare dates, playable artifacts, and competing definitions.
documentary_stories|One Game's Surviving Record|How did one title move from prototype to release and preservation?|Build timeline from builds, manuals, advertising, ports, and archives.
creative_brief|The Original Design Goal|What player experience did one team's brief seek?|Compare pitch, constraints, released build, and contemporary reaction.
materials_and_tools|Cartridge, Disk, or Cabinet|How did physical format affect play and survival?|Examine media, hardware, repair, storage, and access limits.
process_breakdown|A Game From Prototype to Port|Which mechanics changed as one title moved platforms?|Compare versions, developer notes, and technical constraints.
composition_choice|Pixel, Color, and Sound Choices|How did visual and audio design guide play on original hardware?|Analyze output under original display and sound conditions.
collaborative_authorship|Who Built the Classic?|How did programmers, artists, composers, and testers contribute?|Compare credits, artifacts, and attributed testimony.
adaptation_across_media|A Game Becomes a New Form|What changed when one title became a handheld, film, or comic?|Compare rules, narrative, rights, and audience use.
audience_reception|What Players Thought Then|How did initial reception differ from later nostalgia?|Compare period reviews, letters, sales limits, and modern play.
cultural_context|A Game in Its Local Scene|How did arcades, home access, and community norms shape play?|Use bounded location and period with player accounts.
preservation_restoration|Keeping the Original Experience|Which parts of a game are lost when only screenshots survive?|Compare executable, hardware, controls, timing, manuals, and video capture.
rights_and_attribution|Who Can Preserve or Reissue It?|Which rights affect one game's code, art, music, and name?|Check jurisdiction and actual agreements, not assumptions about abandonment.
style_comparison|Two Games Under the Same Limits|Why did two contemporaneous titles solve a design problem differently?|Compare platform, budget, team, mechanic, and player response.
creative_failure|An Ambitious Feature Was Cut|What explains one documented abandoned mechanic?|Compare prototype, limits, schedule, and creator accounts.
field_rules_design|Reading the Original Rules|Do manual and playable version describe the same rules?|Test a lawful copy and record build differences.
field_player_strategy|A Strategy Across Versions|Does a remembered tactic still work in the original release?|Compare rules, timing, and version changes without exploit instructions.
field_difficulty_curve|How Difficulty Was Tuned|How did one old game pace challenge and retries?|Compare levels, lives, player tests where available, and contemporary response.
field_community_norms|Arcade or Fan Practices|How did a local player community establish records or etiquette?|Use dated rules, tournament records, and participant accounts.
field_accessibility_design|Playing an Old Game Today|Which barriers arise from controls, visual cues, audio, or hardware?|Test with defined users and compare lawful adaptation options."""


TABLETOP = """history_origins|Where a Tabletop Game Emerged|Which earlier rules, materials, and communities shaped one game?|Compare dated rulebooks, boards, trade records, and oral history.
famous_examples|A Bestselling Game Examined|Why did one board game spread widely?|Compare distribution, price, rules, marketing, and social context.
hidden_stories|Makers Behind the Box|Whose illustration, playtesting, editing, manufacturing, or translation went uncredited?|Use design files, credits, contracts, and attributed accounts.
beginner_explainers|Learning a Game's Turn|Which information and choices does a player need for one turn?|Explain a named edition using the printed rules and components.
advanced_concepts|Rules Create Incentives|How do scoring and resource rules shape player strategies?|Compare play observations under one edition with a clear example.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Who Invented This Game?|Which evidence supports competing authorship claims?|Compare earliest boards, rules, patents, publications, and oral accounts.
technology_innovation|Printing Changes Play|How did a new material or production method alter one game's cost or reach?|Compare editions, component quality, distribution, and access.
people_personalities|The Designer's Revision|Why did a named designer change one rule?|Use dated prototypes, playtest notes, and collaborators' roles.
major_events|A Rulebook Rewritten|What prompted one significant edition change?|Compare errata, organized play, balance data, and community response.
how_it_works|A Game Round in Practice|How do components, information, and decisions produce an outcome?|Walk through one legal round under a named rule edition.
rise_fall|A Tabletop Game Returns|Why did one game disappear and later reappear?|Compare production, rights, clubs, nostalgia, and new distribution.
then_vs_now|One Game Across Editions|Which rules, art, and player groups changed?|Compare dated editions and actual play experiences.
future_developments|Testing a New Tabletop Edition|What evidence would justify a proposed rule revision?|Define player group, balance measure, access, costs, and playtest plan.
myths_vs_facts|The Ancient Game Claim|Does a marketed origin story match material and textual evidence?|Compare earliest surviving rules and later variants.
documentary_stories|From Prototype to Game Night|How did one title move through testing, publication, and play?|Build a dated record of rules, components, publisher decisions, and reception.
creative_brief|Design for a Table of Players|What experience and session length did a game's original brief target?|Compare prototype goals with published rules and player reports.
materials_and_tools|Board, Cards, and Pieces|How do component size, tactile design, and durability affect play?|Test a named edition with users and production records.
process_breakdown|A Rule's Iterations|How did one mechanic change between prototypes and final edition?|Compare dated rules and playtest feedback.
composition_choice|Information on the Table|How do board layout and icon choices affect decisions?|Compare error rates and comprehension under different versions.
collaborative_authorship|A Game's Many Creators|How did designer, artist, editor, testers, and publisher shape a title?|Trace decisions and credits with documentation.
adaptation_across_media|Tabletop to Digital|What changes when a physical game becomes an app?|Compare rule automation, social interaction, accessibility, and rights.
audience_reception|Who Enjoyed the Game?|What can reviews and play groups establish about reception?|Check sampling, experience level, and edition differences.
cultural_context|A Game in Its Community|How does one tabletop game function at home, club, or festival?|Use consented accounts and avoid treating one setting as universal.
preservation_restoration|Saving a Playable Set|Which materials and instructions must an archive keep?|Preserve board, pieces, rules, edition, box, and play documentation.
rights_and_attribution|Reuse of Rules and Art|Which parts of a game have distinct rights or licensing terms?|Check actual agreements and local law before reprinting.
style_comparison|Two Games With a Shared Mechanic|How do distinct rule contexts change the same mechanic?|Compare player choices, pacing, and outcomes on equal terms.
creative_failure|A Prototype Players Misread|Which rules or components caused confusion in one test?|Use recorded questions and subsequent revisions rather than blame players.
field_rules_design|An Ambiguous Rule Resolved|How does one official clarification change play?|Compare printed text, errata, examples, and a legal game state.
field_player_strategy|Testing a Dominant Strategy|Is one strategy consistently strong across players and starts?|Compare repeated play, player skill, random setup, and counterplay.
field_difficulty_curve|Teaching a Complex Game|Which concepts must newcomers learn first?|Compare onboarding sequences and learner errors in a defined group.
field_community_norms|House Rules and Organized Play|How do local rules differ from an official tournament version?|Attribute local choices and compare effects without ranking legitimacy.
field_accessibility_design|Making Tabletop Play Accessible|Which component or rule barriers limit a defined group?|Test color, print, tactile, turn time, and assistance options with players."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("132", "132_retro_gaming", RETRO,
                  "Historical video games through original builds and hardware, makers, player communities, versions, rights, and preservation.",
                  "original media and hardware, dated manuals and builds, development archives, contemporary reviews, lawful play captures, and attributed developer and player accounts",
                  "Name game, edition or build, platform, region, and date. Distinguish original play from emulation or remaster, credit contributors, and verify rights before reuse.")
    revise_domain("133", "133_board_games_tabletop", TABLETOP,
                  "Board and tabletop games through rules, physical components, makers, play, communities, editions, accessibility, and preservation.",
                  "dated rulebooks and editions, physical game sets, prototypes and playtest records, publisher archives, and attributed player and maker accounts",
                  "Name game, edition, language, and date. Test rules against actual components, credit collaborators, and avoid treating a single group's house rules as universal.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
